# Vercel
.vercel

# Per-user runtime state — pinned prep-brief items and the activity log.
# Not sample data like the rest of data/outputs/, so it shouldn't be tracked.
# One per bank as of 2026-09 (see src/data/workspace_state.py).
data/outputs/*/workspace_state.json

# Cowork/Claude desktop session screenshots (before/after UI captures) --
# generated locally, not project source.
Claude outputs/

# Piper TTS voice models (ONNX weights, tens of MB) -- downloaded locally
# per requirements.txt's instructions, never committed.
data/tts_voices/

# Durable LLM call audit trail (src/audit/llm_audit.py) -- one JSONL file per
# UTC day, generated at runtime, never committed. Same "runtime state, not
# source" reasoning as workspace_state.json above.
data/logs/

# Continuous eval trend (src/agentic/eval_history.py) -- one JSONL per bank,
# generated at runtime every time a real held-out eval computation happens.
# Same "runtime state, not source" reasoning as data/logs/ above.
data/eval_history/

# Cached corpus embedding vectors (src/search/embeddings.py's embed_many
# cache_path) -- a pure, deterministic function of each bank's corpus
# text, regenerated automatically (and correctly, via a content
# fingerprint) whenever it's missing or stale. Multi-MB per bank; nothing
# here is source, just a startup-time optimization.
data/embeddings_cache/

# writable_data_dir()'s own write-probe (src/config/settings.py) -- can land
# in any data/ subdirectory it checks, including ones that ARE otherwise
# tracked (e.g. data/outputs/<bank>/), so this is a blanket rule rather than
# one per directory.
**/.write_probe
